00:31:34.757 --> 00:31:40.202
Is that in this past year as
the United States really grappled with

00:31:40.202 --> 00:31:47.640
who we are as a nation also thinking about
interracial kind of dynamics and systems.

00:31:47.640 --> 00:31:50.555
That allows some communities to thrive,

00:31:50.555 --> 00:31:56.480
well forces others to struggle beyond
what could or should be happening.

00:31:56.480 --> 00:31:59.612
The University at Stanford University
hosted a series of events

00:31:59.612 --> 00:32:01.160
called brave spaces.

00:32:01.160 --> 00:32:05.293
I was a facilitator for these
conversations, intentional spaces for

00:32:05.293 --> 00:32:07.370
us to talk about race.

00:32:07.370 --> 00:32:09.250
Difference, justice.

00:32:09.250 --> 00:32:10.550
What does that mean?

00:32:10.550 --> 00:32:12.760
How have we experienced it as individuals?

00:32:12.760 --> 00:32:17.781
And how can we bring this conversation
kind of to the forefront of what we do,

00:32:17.781 --> 00:32:22.566
such that the university can be a more
inclusive space where we can really

00:32:22.566 --> 00:32:25.482
work and operate to our fullest potential?

00:32:25.482 --> 00:32:28.668
And so, do this exercise,
come up with that,

00:32:28.668 --> 00:32:32.429
these lists of things about
who you are and sometimes,

00:32:32.429 --> 00:32:37.820
you might have a stroke of
inspiration somewhere, bring that in.

00:32:37.820 --> 00:32:41.076
If you're thinking, hey,
is this important for the application,

00:32:41.076 --> 00:32:44.530
let's take a look at
the criteria that Stanford uses.

00:32:44.530 --> 00:32:46.060
How might this connect?

00:32:46.060 --> 00:32:50.090
What's an example for
how this came out in the real world?

00:32:50.090 --> 00:32:53.762
And then that could be one way
that you start to identify, okay,

00:32:53.762 --> 00:32:58.183
here are some things that I really want to
make sure come out in my application.

00:32:58.183 --> 00:33:01.101
Here are some of those landmarks
that I want to provide,

00:33:01.101 --> 00:33:05.353
so that while I'm navigating this as
an applicant, whoever is reading this can

00:33:05.353 --> 00:33:09.287
also navigate the course and journey of
my life in a way that they are seeing

00:33:09.287 --> 00:33:13.930
the things that have really shaped who
I am and how I'm going to show up.

00:33:13.930 --> 00:33:15.650
So, tips.

00:33:15.650 --> 00:33:18.618
We are getting close, I want to make
sure we get through these tips and so

00:33:18.618 --> 00:33:20.970
that I can jump into that Q&amp;A box.

00:33:20.970 --> 00:33:24.090
If you have questions,
go ahead and add them here.

00:33:24.090 --> 00:33:26.620
We also have an up voting feature.

00:33:26.620 --> 00:33:30.502
So go ahead if there is a question that
you find really resonates for you,

00:33:30.502 --> 00:33:35.415
click that thumbs up button, it's going to
help elevate that question to the top.

00:33:35.415 --> 00:33:38.908
I'm going to do my best to answer as many
questions as I can with our final ten

00:33:38.908 --> 00:33:40.360
minutes together.

00:33:40.360 --> 00:33:44.558
For some of them, I might be refer you to
some other events throughout this week,

00:33:44.558 --> 00:33:47.299
and others,
I'm really going to try and unpack it.

00:33:47.299 --> 00:33:52.362
Some of this philosophical and background
understanding level to help provide

00:33:52.362 --> 00:33:58.180
that understanding and process based
approach, as opposed to just the output.

00:33:58.180 --> 00:34:00.991
One of my colleagues talked about this and

00:34:00.991 --> 00:34:06.800
talked about how are we coaching you
to self coach through this process?

00:34:06.800 --> 00:34:11.371
How can we give you the tools and
knowledge and tool kits, so

00:34:11.371 --> 00:34:16.135
that you can be your best self
advocate through this journey?

00:34:16.135 --> 00:34:18.660
So, let's get to those tips.

00:34:18.660 --> 00:34:22.059
We're going to do a little bit
unpacking and then get to the Q&amp;A.

00:34:22.059 --> 00:34:25.268
So first, own your journey.

00:34:25.268 --> 00:34:29.731
No two people came to the GSB
following the same trajectory.

00:34:29.731 --> 00:34:36.331
Everybody does think a little bit
differently, know yours, celebrate yours.

00:34:36.331 --> 00:34:40.767
You'd be surprised at how often
the things that you do every day,

00:34:40.767 --> 00:34:43.672
probably without even thinking about it,

00:34:43.672 --> 00:34:48.531
are some of the most fascinating
things to us, on the admissions side.

00:34:48.531 --> 00:34:51.900
The things like,
how do you operate within a team?

00:34:51.900 --> 00:34:54.860
Maybe it's the way that you interact
with the people around you.

00:34:54.860 --> 00:35:01.612
You don't often think twice about it,
it doesn't always come up with an award,

00:35:01.612 --> 00:35:05.697
or achievement, or
something that defines it.

00:35:05.697 --> 00:35:10.250
But that is a doublesome ways to lead,
right?

00:35:10.250 --> 00:35:15.224
So really take that step back,
kind of release whatever notions you

00:35:15.224 --> 00:35:20.109
might have heard about what quote
unquote leadership looks like,

00:35:20.109 --> 00:35:25.257
release whatever ideas you have
about what admissions wants to hear,

00:35:25.257 --> 00:35:28.230
and take control of your story.

00:35:28.230 --> 00:35:34.670
This is me, this is what I want to tell
the MBA admissions office about myself.

00:35:34.670 --> 00:35:38.762
As you take control of this journey,
no one can tell you how or

00:35:38.762 --> 00:35:41.430
what you should be saying, right?

00:35:41.430 --> 00:35:45.850
People can give input or
folks can provide some coaching, but

00:35:45.850 --> 00:35:49.390
ultimately, you are the expert in you.

00:35:49.390 --> 00:35:51.378
So let that come to the forefront and

00:35:51.378 --> 00:35:54.720
really anchor on the things
that matter to you.

00:35:54.720 --> 00:35:59.943
One of the things that I often see,
which is often a missed opportunity,

00:35:59.943 --> 00:36:05.210
I would say is, it can be really
tempting to look at different models.

00:36:05.210 --> 00:36:07.453
Here's the thing that got me in or

00:36:07.453 --> 00:36:11.550
this is what you're supposed to
do XYZ to get into Stanford.

00:36:12.850 --> 00:36:17.297
Because each one of you is different,
because each one of you brings

00:36:17.297 --> 00:36:22.371
a different lived experience and
skill set of competencies for leadership,

00:36:22.371 --> 00:36:27.305
action, whatever lenses you bring,
that might have worked for someone.

00:36:27.305 --> 00:36:31.281
And if you try to mold yourself to
that sometimes the things that make

00:36:31.281 --> 00:36:35.745
you the most effective, or the elements
about you that can really be the most

00:36:35.745 --> 00:36:39.096
impactful in a business school
application or journey,

00:36:39.096 --> 00:36:42.904
you might lose those because
you're trying to be someone else.

00:36:42.904 --> 00:36:44.637
We're celebrating you.

00:36:44.637 --> 00:36:48.900
Your classmates are going to be
learning from you, so own this journey.

00:36:50.620 --> 00:36:53.550
Find value in the process and
not just the outcome.

00:36:53.550 --> 00:36:55.690
And we're going to go
a little bit better here.

00:36:55.690 --> 00:37:00.453
I mean this both in terms of
the outcome of the application process,

00:37:00.453 --> 00:37:04.215
yes, admission would be great,
and the reality is,

00:37:04.215 --> 00:37:08.050
that is not going to be the outcome for
everyone.

00:37:08.050 --> 00:37:12.875
That said, this process going through
the exercise of understanding

00:37:12.875 --> 00:37:17.779
what matters to you, these are things
that can help guide you as you come

00:37:17.779 --> 00:37:21.410
to different decision points in your life.

00:37:21.410 --> 00:37:24.470
Maybe you have two jobs that
you might be considering.

00:37:24.470 --> 00:37:25.963
How do you choose which one?

00:37:25.963 --> 00:37:28.283
Maybe it's by going with
what matters to you.

00:37:28.283 --> 00:37:31.000
Maybe there's an ethical
dilemma that you're facing.

00:37:31.000 --> 00:37:35.451
Let's go back to these core mission
pieces and values that you hold to

00:37:35.451 --> 00:37:39.920
help guide you through some of
these kind of points in life.

00:37:39.920 --> 00:37:45.131
So even beyond the application outcome,
there is still value behind going

00:37:45.131 --> 00:37:51.430
through it and really taking the moment to
process and allow yourself to go there.

00:37:51.430 --> 00:37:55.921
Think about this beyond just the pure
functionality of getting in, but rather,

00:37:55.921 --> 00:38:00.215
maybe even think about it as a coaching
exercise that you are guiding yourself

00:38:00.215 --> 00:38:00.825
through.

00:38:00.825 --> 00:38:03.078
As for the things in your application,

00:38:03.078 --> 00:38:07.770
you can also think about this as not
just the outcome, but how did you do it?

00:38:07.770 --> 00:38:11.370
Coming back to that DLP
demonstrated leadership potential.

00:38:11.370 --> 00:38:13.296
What did you do and how?

00:38:13.296 --> 00:38:15.030
What was the setting around it?

00:38:15.030 --> 00:38:16.390
Who else was involved?

00:38:16.390 --> 00:38:17.760
What happened next?

00:38:17.760 --> 00:38:19.100
Tell me more.

00:38:19.100 --> 00:38:24.461
That is one of my favorite questions kind
of talking to folks that tell me more, and

00:38:24.461 --> 00:38:30.840
so I really encourage you to take a moment
to remember, reflect, process, connect.

00:38:30.840 --> 00:38:34.693
So remember the things that happened,
things that you're proud of,

00:38:34.693 --> 00:38:37.020
reflect on the situation around it.

00:38:37.020 --> 00:38:41.196
I mentioned some instances that could or
some elements that could be handy, but

00:38:41.196 --> 00:38:44.078
also reflect on how you were
feeling in those moments.

00:38:44.078 --> 00:38:45.458
What were you challenged by?

00:38:45.458 --> 00:38:48.450
What were you energized by process?

00:38:50.250 --> 00:38:54.310
Take a moment and think about how
these things connect to each other.

00:38:54.310 --> 00:38:58.450
In all actuality, I probably should
have ordered it as remember, reflect,

00:38:58.450 --> 00:39:02.526
connect process, but I have to, [LAUGH]
I admit and in full disclosure here,

00:39:02.526 --> 00:39:06.313
remember reflect, process,
connect is so much easier to remember.

00:39:06.313 --> 00:39:09.893
But we can say those processing
connect pieces built together connect

00:39:09.893 --> 00:39:11.190
the dots, right?

00:39:11.190 --> 00:39:13.850
Because of this, that happened.

00:39:13.850 --> 00:39:16.059
I was inspired by, XYZ.

00:39:16.059 --> 00:39:19.700
See how these elements
connect to who you are today.

00:39:19.700 --> 00:39:21.710
I learned this, I applied it there.

00:39:23.010 --> 00:39:26.737
And that process piece take time to
process how all of these different

00:39:26.737 --> 00:39:28.040
dots connect.

00:39:28.040 --> 00:39:31.060
There might be dots that
you never realized existed.

00:39:31.060 --> 00:39:33.240
Maybe it's through that
exercise we did today.

00:39:33.240 --> 00:39:36.853
Maybe you didn't know that you
really did engage with baldness at

00:39:36.853 --> 00:39:39.060
an intellectual level.

00:39:39.060 --> 00:39:44.620
Give yourself time to unpack,
celebrate, and explore through this.

00:39:44.620 --> 00:39:48.980
And remember, through all of it,
it all begins with you.

00:39:48.980 --> 00:39:53.220
Okay, so
that is what I have prepared right now.

00:39:53.220 --> 00:39:56.070
So I'm going to jump into our Q&amp;A box.

00:39:56.070 --> 00:40:00.716
Before we do that, I really want to
encourage everybody here to continue your

00:40:00.716 --> 00:40:02.612
journey at MyStanford.mba.

00:40:02.612 --> 00:40:06.840
And with some short questions, we're able
to create a dashboard that will help,

00:40:06.840 --> 00:40:10.734
Consolidate some of the events that
may be of most interest to you.

00:40:10.734 --> 00:40:15.122
There is also an application tracker
to help keep you kind of up to date on

00:40:15.122 --> 00:40:18.207
where you are and
get you go into that finish line.

00:40:18.207 --> 00:40:22.412
I really encourage you,
if you aren't sure whether or

00:40:22.412 --> 00:40:27.541
not you should apply now or
in the future, take a moment and think.

00:40:27.541 --> 00:40:29.770
What is it that you want to do?

00:40:29.770 --> 00:40:32.225
How can Stanford get you there?

00:40:32.225 --> 00:40:36.623
If you're thinking we can,
I encourage you, go ahead,

00:40:36.623 --> 00:40:42.228
do this process, take these moments
to really celebrate your journey.

00:40:42.228 --> 00:40:45.944
Because tomorrow can be
a very beautiful thing and

00:40:45.944 --> 00:40:51.620
I want to make sure that you give yourself
every opportunity to realize that.

00:40:51.620 --> 00:40:55.553
So let me go ahead,
we are going to jump into that Q&amp;A box.

00:40:55.553 --> 00:40:58.571
So I'm going to stop sharing for
a moment and here we go.

00:40:58.571 --> 00:41:00.654
So here's a question from Anna.

00:41:00.654 --> 00:41:05.375
A number of you have also kind
of bumped this question up.

00:41:05.375 --> 00:41:09.514
So Anna imagines that the GSB like
other business schools tries to admit

00:41:09.514 --> 00:41:10.553
a diverse class.

00:41:10.553 --> 00:41:15.381
How does that affect how they try to
balance students from different countries,

00:41:15.381 --> 00:41:16.593
industries, etc.

00:41:16.593 --> 00:41:18.400
So great question here.

00:41:18.400 --> 00:41:19.652
I think ultimately,

00:41:19.652 --> 00:41:23.555
the one number that we're trying
to target is bringing in a class.

00:41:23.555 --> 00:41:27.267
So for
us that is still 20-ish year to year.

00:41:27.267 --> 00:41:31.985
And even less if Lexis depending
on the circumstances, right?

00:41:31.985 --> 00:41:36.871
But rather than focusing on that number or
is there some breakdown that we're

00:41:36.871 --> 00:41:40.943
going towards, we're really
looking at you as an individual.

00:41:40.943 --> 00:41:47.299
One of the kind of amazing things that
I really appreciate about the holistic

00:41:47.299 --> 00:41:53.358
review process is that we don't think
about you as someone from x place,

00:41:53.358 --> 00:41:59.144
but how does being from x place shape
the perspective that you bring?

00:41:59.144 --> 00:42:02.833
And I think if you allow
yourself to take a step and

00:42:02.833 --> 00:42:07.603
look at it from that perspective,
you're going to have a lot more

00:42:07.603 --> 00:42:12.283
agency in demonstrating to us
that perspective that enhances

00:42:12.283 --> 00:42:17.506
dialogue to the classroom or
spark conversations in the community.

00:42:17.506 --> 00:42:21.094
This might sound like a little bit
of a tangent of an answer, but

00:42:21.094 --> 00:42:25.838
something that we talked about, something
that Dean Moss has talked to me about and

00:42:25.838 --> 00:42:30.067
we've had conversations about this is,
staying on your side of the net.

00:42:30.067 --> 00:42:31.844
What does that mean, right?

00:42:31.844 --> 00:42:34.825
If you think about a game like tennis or
volleyball,

00:42:34.825 --> 00:42:38.432
you are in control of what's
happening on your side of the net.

00:42:38.432 --> 00:42:43.368
What's happening and what the other
person decides to do, that's up to them.

00:42:43.368 --> 00:42:48.740
So as we think about this application
process, my goal with this week is to

00:42:48.740 --> 00:42:54.373
bring more light and visibility to what
are the pieces on your side of the net so

00:42:54.373 --> 00:42:58.297
that you can understand,
okay, here are the steps.

00:42:58.297 --> 00:43:00.915
I can take left, right, around.

00:43:00.915 --> 00:43:04.827
And so not that I'm trying to
give a non-answer answer, but

00:43:04.827 --> 00:43:09.589
at a practical sense, there's actually
a whole field called enrollment

00:43:09.589 --> 00:43:13.066
management where this is
part of the consideration.

00:43:13.066 --> 00:43:17.161
How are we bringing in as
diverse cohort as possible?

00:43:17.161 --> 00:43:20.576
I think one of the lucky things for
us is that we do get a really broad

00:43:20.576 --> 00:43:24.570
representation of extremely talented
individuals from around the world.

00:43:24.570 --> 00:43:27.421
That said, sometimes I do
get the question, why are so

00:43:27.421 --> 00:43:29.344
many people from the United States?

00:43:29.344 --> 00:43:32.093
Or why are they so
many people from consulting?

00:43:32.093 --> 00:43:36.611
Is that going to be a disadvantage for me?

00:43:36.611 --> 00:43:40.566
Part of this is that those tend to
be some of our largest pipelines.

00:43:40.566 --> 00:43:43.427
We can only admit the people who apply.

00:43:43.427 --> 00:43:47.349
And so that is that other part of
encouraging you to take a step.

00:43:47.349 --> 00:43:50.523
And if this is something
that you're thinking about,

00:43:50.523 --> 00:43:55.007
don't count yourself out because you
don't immediately identify with what

00:43:55.007 --> 00:43:57.565
it looks like on our class profile, right?

00:43:57.565 --> 00:44:00.729
So couple different layers to that answer.

00:44:00.729 --> 00:44:03.951
We really do care about the individual and
the talents that you bring.

00:44:03.951 --> 00:44:08.588
We will never admit someone just
because of one thing, right?

00:44:08.588 --> 00:44:10.978
And so regardless of where you come from,

00:44:10.978 --> 00:44:14.341
hopefully you're able to share
all of these pieces of us.

00:44:14.341 --> 00:44:18.859
So build that case for
saying this is a compelling individual.

00:44:18.859 --> 00:44:20.402
Thank you for that question, Anna.

00:44:20.402 --> 00:44:25.047
From Deshaun, talking about very
themes that are within the bounds

00:44:25.047 --> 00:44:27.425
of including in the application.

00:44:27.425 --> 00:44:32.290
Can we touch upon what applicants should
avoid creating their application?

00:44:32.290 --> 00:44:36.992
This might be useful for internationals
who might not be very familiar with the US

00:44:36.992 --> 00:44:39.355
admissions process and expectations.

00:44:39.355 --> 00:44:41.394
Thank you, Deshaun, for this question.

00:44:41.394 --> 00:44:46.534
This is at the heart of
what we are trying to do.

00:44:46.534 --> 00:44:52.481
I would say there is very little that
is off limits for the application.

00:44:52.481 --> 00:44:55.930
So there might be a topic that
might feel controversial.

00:44:55.930 --> 00:45:01.465
There might be a event in your life
that might not seem immediately

00:45:01.465 --> 00:45:07.618
business related, but it really is
important to how you view yourself.

00:45:07.618 --> 00:45:09.909
When it comes to the GSB application,

00:45:09.909 --> 00:45:12.922
and I can't speak to all
applications out there.

00:45:12.922 --> 00:45:17.666
But when it comes to the GSB application,
think about it as what

00:45:17.666 --> 00:45:22.962
you're writing about is almost less
important than the so what of it.

00:45:22.962 --> 00:45:25.662
What are you trying to
convey about yourself?

00:45:25.662 --> 00:45:31.935
Or who are you because of x, y, or z
things that you're trying to write about?

00:45:31.935 --> 00:45:34.878
And so
as long as that topic is in good taste,

00:45:34.878 --> 00:45:39.494
and here's maybe one guideline that
you might take home with you is,

00:45:39.494 --> 00:45:43.806
if you step back, and
let's talk about the essays for a second.

00:45:43.806 --> 00:45:49.165
If by the end of that essay, I know more
about that topic than I do about you,

00:45:49.165 --> 00:45:53.930
or how you engage with a topic,
how that shapes your perspective,

00:45:53.930 --> 00:45:55.907
what you've done with it.

00:45:55.907 --> 00:45:59.807
If I knew more about that topic than you,
some element of you,

00:45:59.807 --> 00:46:04.306
that might be the moment to step back and
do a little bit of assessment and

00:46:04.306 --> 00:46:06.409
shift kind of your angle on that.

00:46:06.409 --> 00:46:11.258
So ultimately very little is off
the rails here [LAUGH] in this process,

00:46:11.258 --> 00:46:15.203
which is both empowering and
a little bit intimidating,

00:46:15.203 --> 00:46:18.178
not everything has to deal with business.

00:46:18.178 --> 00:46:23.963
Again, thinking about how the individual
and what you bring to the table is so

00:46:23.963 --> 00:46:28.159
much more than kind of the class
that you might be taking.

00:46:28.159 --> 00:46:31.349
You are so much more than a test score or
transcript,

00:46:31.349 --> 00:46:33.896
how can we recognize and celebrate that?

00:46:33.896 --> 00:46:37.170
So that's a very high level answer.

00:46:37.170 --> 00:46:38.419
Through this week,

00:46:38.419 --> 00:46:42.977
we're actually going to dig into all
of these elements very specifically.

00:46:42.977 --> 00:46:47.326
And I'm really looking forward to
our panels because I'm excited for

00:46:47.326 --> 00:46:49.233
the conversations to come.

00:46:49.233 --> 00:46:51.707
Okay, all right.

00:46:51.707 --> 00:46:54.316
Question here and
this is more tactical practical.

00:46:54.316 --> 00:46:55.595
When does it matter?

00:46:55.595 --> 00:46:58.540
Round one, round two,
no major difference here.

00:46:58.540 --> 00:47:01.790
And we'll also be talking about some
of that tactical practical with

00:47:01.790 --> 00:47:03.145
the connecting of the dots.

